WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.190
A stage backdrop: a
bare field, a grey sky,

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.100
and two small figures standing in front.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:08.410
Look closer.

4
00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.240
The painted soil is chalk and flint.

5
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:13.140
The sky is heavy.

6
00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:15.510
The crop has been eaten bare.

7
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.210
Two small figures, one huge field.

8
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:22.800
So what if a novel's landscape
is more than scenery?

9
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:25.120
In this mission, you'll meet ecocriticism,

10
00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.570
and the questions it asks
about a novel's land.

11
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:31.540
You'll stand with two women
hacking at a swede-field,

12
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.550
high on a chalk upland.

13
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.000
And you'll weigh two ways
of reading that same field.

14
00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:41.870
Your mission: work out what changes when
the landscape is more than a backdrop.
